KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.variadic]/4-5.  A pack expansion whose pattern is a
`sizeof` unary-expression (`sizeof(Us)...`), forwarded from an enclosing function
template, expands to the wrong element count: `box<sizeof(Us)...>::n` (n =
sizeof...(Vs)) evaluated in `chk((char)1,(char)2)` is not 2.  A member-value
pattern `box<Trait<Us>::v...>` forwarded the same way expands correctly
(cpp11_nontype_value_pack_fn_template, CORE), so the defect is specific to the
`sizeof(Us)...` sizeof-expression pattern.  Residual non-type-pack defect from
reproducing the tuple _TupleConstraints shape with a non-type proxy (the tuple
uses TYPE packs; cpp11_alias_template_parallel_pack is CORE).  Flip to CORE once
a forwarded `sizeof(Us)...` pack expansion has the correct arity.
